    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the single `AcceptanceTest` covers this behavior).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the audit-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- A single-responsibility step that logs one line via the SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`, containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`:\n- Added an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`. It runs after `save` so the DB-generated `id` is populated, and reuses the same governed transaction as the surrounding steps.\n\nDesign notes: I kept the logic in its own small function class rather than folding it into `SaveOwner` or `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, matching the project's one-function-per-step convention and keeping each class focused. The audit reads the already-published `Owner` variable via `@Val` \u2014 no new state or duplication. `LocalDate.toString()` yields the same ISO date text (`2026-09-16`) the response DTO serializes, so the emitted line satisfies the test's `anyContains(id, customerCode, registrationDate)` check.\n\nAll tests pass, and the AUDIT line is visible in the run output:\n`INFO  AUDIT - Created owner id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-16`",
